<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Sirmur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1095 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Nahan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Rajput hill state of the Shivaliks ruled from Nahan, whose name was given to the Sirmoor Battalion, the first of the British Army's Gurkha regiments.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling Prakash dynasty traditionally dates its rule to 1095, when a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> prince settled in the hills between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a>. Raja Karam Prakash founded the town of Nahan as the capital in 1621.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sirmur's Rajas held a strategic position on the routes from the plains to the hills and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doon-valley">Doon</a> valley. Like its neighbours it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gurkhas</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a>, from 1803 to 1815. Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamsher-prakash">Shamsher Prakash</a> (r. 1856–1898) modernised the state, founding the Nahan Foundry and building roads and schools.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The British restored the dynasty in 1815 and raised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/2nd-king-edward-viis-own-gurkha-rifles">Sirmoor Battalion</a> there from former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gurkha</a> soldiers. Sirmur merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> in April 1948 and is now Sirmaur district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sirmur-state.jpg" alt="Sirmur State" width="320" height="258"><figcaption>Image: Indus Publishing Company, New Delhi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Sirmur_State,_Indus_Publishing_Company,_New_Delhi,_1934.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1095 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nahan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karam Prakash, Shamsher Prakash</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sirmauri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sirmaur, Nahan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1522&amp;focus=sirmur-state" aria-label="Sirmur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6683 1063 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sirmur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7003 1319L7364 1601M7003 1319L7364 1602M7003 1319L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7003 1319h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7003 1319h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nahan. <a href="/atlas?year=1522&amp;focus=sirmur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
